{
  "dom_id": "step-q336142",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "The position $x$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by \n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2}-24\\sqrt[3]{t},\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity at time $t=8.$\n\n$v(8)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The velocity is the derivative of the position function $x(t)$ with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-24\\sqrt[3]{t}) \\\\  & =2t-24\\cdot \\frac{1}{3{(\\sqrt[3]{t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =2t-\\frac{8}{{(\\sqrt[3]{t})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=8,$ we substitute $t=8$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(8) & =2(8)-\\frac{8}{{(\\sqrt[3]{8})}^{2}} \\\\  & =16-2 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
